Today, 20% of trucks run empty or partially loaded, also many private entities travel with no passengers in their cars. A possible solution to avoid inefficiency are collaborative platforms. Here, logistics companies or private entities can offer and provide logistics services to other private entities or companies. Platforms operate and build large, scalable user networks and resources accessible on demand. The platform is used between individuals as a meeting place where they can arrange the transportation of goods. In particular design for crowd logistics means to organize and maximize the transportation of goods in many alternative ways. The added value of using these platforms is that all the goods are insured and significant reductions in emissions can be achieved. 

A good case study for this strategy is www.shiply.com